  2574	# PLAN-177 W1 (CF-9): `.claude/.gitignore`, a NEW framework-delivered file.
  2575	#
  2576	# The two blocks above land in the adopter's ROOT .gitignore, which a
  2577	# `--ceremony user` install never touches (WS4: a user install writes inside
  2578	# .claude/ and nowhere else). So the exact population that /night-mode most
  2579	# affects — user-ceremony adopters — had no protection at all, the damage the
  2580	# GA re-pass names in verdict-ga-1.txt:5. This file lives INSIDE .claude/, so
  2581	# it is delivered in EVERY ceremony without violating that invariant (the
  2582	# smoke-install.yml user-ceremony assert allows .claude and .git at top level).
  2583	#
