Applicable conditions for this payload: 1, 5–14, 24, 31, 33–35, 42, 45, 47–48, 56, 60–64, 73–76, 81–82 and 84. Conditions 3 and 7 concern link-mode installs, outside the stated cohort.

### Findings

- P1 annex — declared condition 42. FILE:LINE: [scripts/upgrade.sh:4951](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:4951>), [scripts/upgrade.sh:4979](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:4979>). Concrete failure: a v1.3.0 adopter-authored `docs/` or `.github/` file that happens to equal a historical template is classified as “pristine prior generation,” overwritten and registered as framework-owned despite having no prior manifest record. Later upgrades rewrite it, doctor treats edits as drift, and uninstall may delete it. Minimal fix: require prior delivery evidence, not historical byte equality, before refresh and registration.

