No P0 and no declared condition is false. For the stated v1.3.0 maintainer/copy-mode cohort, the envelope is honest and sufficient only when its preflights are followed literally; the scripts are not safe by default.

Applicable conditions: 1, 5–6, 8–14, 24, 31, 33–35, 42, 45, 47–48, 56, 60–64, 73–76, 81–82 and 84. Conditions 3 and 7 are link-mode-only.

### Findings

- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared conditions 5 and 42. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:1913`, `scripts/install.sh:1923`, `scripts/upgrade.sh:4951`, `scripts/upgrade.sh:4979`. Concrete failure: an adopter-authored `docs/` or `.github/` file byte-equal to the current or a historical template is registered or refreshed as framework-owned without prior delivery evidence. Later upgrades rewrite it, doctor treats edits as drift, and uninstall may delete it. Minimal fix: require a prior valid delivery record; byte equality alone must never establish ownership.

- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared condition 64. FILE:LINE: `scripts/upgrade.sh:1620`, `scripts/upgrade.sh:1660`. Concrete failure: if an adopter owns a path newly introduced by v1.4.0, such as `check_compact_pinning.py`, missing baseline evidence produces `FALLBACK`, which overwrites even under `--on-conflict=refuse` and transfers ownership to the framework. Minimal fix: classify “new source + existing destination + no prior record” as `CONFLICT`.

- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared conditions 8, 34 and 45. FILE:LINE: `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:1311`, `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:1333`, `scripts/install.sh:1804`, `scripts/install.sh:1841`, `scripts/install.sh:3556`, `scripts/install.sh:3697`. Concrete failure: an unusable route table causes the manifest writer to return success without provenance; a missing, non-regular or refused source is only `SKIP`. The remaining install proceeds, records `install_succeeded:true`, prints “Install complete,” and exits 0. Minimal fix: validate the table and every route source before the first write; persist failure and return nonzero for any rejected or absent route.

- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared conditions 47 and 48. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:1453`, `scripts/install.sh:1470`, `scripts/install.sh:1473`, `scripts/install.sh:2401`. Concrete failure: `install_dispatcher` follows destination symlinks and unconditionally overwrites adopter-edited dispatcher files; the predictable deny-baseline tempfile can also redirect a write outside the target. Minimal fix: put these writes behind the shared confinement/provenance preflight and use exclusively created same-directory staging followed by atomic rename.

- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared condition 73. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:496`, `scripts/install.sh:705`, `scripts/install.sh:1206`, `scripts/install.sh:1334`. Concrete failure: `--profile` is split without grammar validation and interpolated into source and destination paths. A traversal value whose computed source exists can make `install_one` copy outside the target. Minimal fix: accept only documented single-segment profile names before any target mutation and confine every derived destination.

- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared condition 75. FILE:LINE: `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:158`, `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:178`, `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:251`. Concrete failure: manifest generation walks target directories, so an adopter’s untouched `.claude/hooks/acme_local.py` can be recorded with its own hash as framework-owned and later removed by uninstall. Minimal fix: generate the manifest from an exact ledger of files actually delivered or whose ownership continuity was proven.

### NEW FINDINGS (annex)

No new undeclared P1.

- SEVERITY: P1 annex carried from rc.1 and re-reported because it is reachable on the mainline fresh-install path. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:771`, `scripts/install.sh:792`, `scripts/install.sh:1994`, `scripts/install.sh:3619`. Concrete failure: an unwritable `.github/` can make CODEOWNERS staging fail after `.claude/` and `docs/` were written. The final status is nonzero, but rollback covers only a pre-existing `.claude`; a fresh target remains partially installed without manifest or install-state. Minimal fix: pre-stage all outputs before mutation or maintain a complete rollback ledger for every created path.

