   274	The append path has the mirror-image race: the previous HMAC is read before
   275	the log lock is taken, so two parallel writers (two sessions, or two parallel
   276	agent spawns of one session) can chain to the same predecessor, and
   277	`verify_chain()` then reports a break nobody caused. The chain is proof of
   278	integrity only for stretches written by one writer at a time; detection of a
   279	break still holds, the absence of false breaks under concurrent writers does
   280	not (signed condition of rc.1).
