.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r5/verdict-ga-2.txt:7:- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared conditions 5 and 42. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:1913`, `scripts/install.sh:1923`, `scripts/upgrade.sh:4951`, `scripts/upgrade.sh:4979`. Concrete failure: an adopter-authored `docs/` or `.github/` file byte-equal to the current or a historical template is registered or refreshed as framework-owned without prior delivery evidence. Later upgrades rewrite it, doctor treats edits as drift, and uninstall may delete it. Minimal fix: require a prior valid delivery record; byte equality alone must never establish ownership.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r5/verdict-ga-2.txt:11:- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared conditions 8, 34 and 45. FILE:LINE: `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:1311`, `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:1333`, `scripts/install.sh:1804`, `scripts/install.sh:1841`, `scripts/install.sh:3556`, `scripts/install.sh:3697`. Concrete failure: an unusable route table causes the manifest writer to return success without provenance; a missing, non-regular or refused source is only `SKIP`. The remaining install proceeds, records `install_succeeded:true`, prints “Install complete,” and exits 0. Minimal fix: validate the table and every route source before the first write; persist failure and return nonzero for any rejected or absent route.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r5/verdict-ga-2.txt:13:- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared conditions 47 and 48. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:1453`, `scripts/install.sh:1470`, `scripts/install.sh:1473`, `scripts/install.sh:2401`. Concrete failure: `install_dispatcher` follows destination symlinks and unconditionally overwrites adopter-edited dispatcher files; the predictable deny-baseline tempfile can also redirect a write outside the target. Minimal fix: put these writes behind the shared confinement/provenance preflight and use exclusively created same-directory staging followed by atomic rename.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r5/verdict-ga-2.txt:15:- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared condition 73. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:496`, `scripts/install.sh:705`, `scripts/install.sh:1206`, `scripts/install.sh:1334`. Concrete failure: `--profile` is split without grammar validation and interpolated into source and destination paths. A traversal value whose computed source exists can make `install_one` copy outside the target. Minimal fix: accept only documented single-segment profile names before any target mutation and confine every derived destination.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r5/verdict-ga-2.txt:17:- SEVERITY: P1 annex — declared condition 75. FILE:LINE: `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:158`, `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:178`, `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:251`. Concrete failure: manifest generation walks target directories, so an adopter’s untouched `.claude/hooks/acme_local.py` can be recorded with its own hash as framework-owned and later removed by uninstall. Minimal fix: generate the manifest from an exact ledger of files actually delivered or whose ownership continuity was proven.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r5/verdict-ga-2.txt:23:- SEVERITY: P1 annex carried from rc.1 and re-reported because it is reachable on the mainline fresh-install path. FILE:LINE: `scripts/install.sh:771`, `scripts/install.sh:792`, `scripts/install.sh:1994`, `scripts/install.sh:3619`. Concrete failure: an unwritable `.github/` can make CODEOWNERS staging fail after `.claude/` and `docs/` were written. The final status is nonzero, but rollback covers only a pre-existing `.claude`; a fresh target remains partially installed without manifest or install-state. Minimal fix: pre-stage all outputs before mutation or maintain a complete rollback ledger for every created path.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r4/verdict-ga-2.txt:7:- P1 annex — declared condition 42. FILE:LINE: [scripts/upgrade.sh:4951](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:4951>), [scripts/upgrade.sh:4979](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:4979>). Concrete failure: a v1.3.0 adopter-authored `docs/` or `.github/` file that happens to equal a historical template is classified as “pristine prior generation,” overwritten and registered as framework-owned despite having no prior manifest record. Later upgrades rewrite it, doctor treats edits as drift, and uninstall may delete it. Minimal fix: require prior delivery evidence, not historical byte equality, before refresh and registration.
