.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r4/verdict-ga-2.txt:13:- P1 annex — declared condition 73. FILE:LINE: [scripts/install.sh:496](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/install.sh:496>), [scripts/install.sh:705](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/install.sh:705>), [scripts/install.sh:1334](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/install.sh:1334>), [scripts/install.sh:1206](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/install.sh:1206>). Concrete failure: `--profile` is split without grammar validation and interpolated into both source and destination paths; a traversal value whose computed source exists can make `install_one` copy outside the target. Minimal fix: accept only single-segment profile names matching the documented allowlist before any write, and run every derived destination through the confinement predicate.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r4/verdict-ga-2.txt:15:- P1 annex carried from rc.1; re-reported because it is reachable on the mainline fresh-install path. FILE:LINE: [scripts/install.sh:771](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/install.sh:771>), [scripts/install.sh:1994](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/install.sh:1994>), [scripts/install.sh:3619](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.Mxwo9C/wt/scripts/install.sh:3619>). Concrete failure: on a fresh install, a late CODEOWNERS staging failure—such as an unwritable `.github/`—is accumulated after `.claude/` and `docs/` have already been written. The final rc is nonzero, but rollback restores only a pre-existing `.claude` snapshot; a fresh target remains partially installed without manifest or install-state. Minimal fix: pre-stage/preflight all writes or maintain a complete mutation ledger capable of rolling back every created target path.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r2/verdict-ga-2.txt:7:- **P1 signed known-open — condition 42 — [scripts/upgrade.sh:4951](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.nb1a8y/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:4951).** A v1.3.0 adopter-authored `docs/rotation-log.md` byte-identical to a historical framework generation has no manifest provenance, but is classified as “pristine prior generation,” replaced, and registered as framework-owned at lines 4979–4992. A later repair can overwrite it and uninstall can delete it. Minimal fix: require prior delivery evidence, not historical byte equality, before changing ownership.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r2/verdict-ga-2.txt:11:- **P1 signed known-open — conditions 8, 34 and 45 — [scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:1333](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.nb1a8y/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:1333), [scripts/install.sh:3634](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.nb1a8y/wt/scripts/install.sh:3634).** An unusable route table makes the manifest writer report an error but return success; a missing/non-regular route source is skipped. The installer can then write successful install-state and print “Install complete” without a usable provenance manifest. Minimal fix: validate the table and every required source before the first target write, then persist failure and exit nonzero on any rejection.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r2/verdict-ga-2.txt:15:- **P1 annex carried from rc.1; mainline-install reachable — [scripts/install.sh:771](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.nb1a8y/wt/scripts/install.sh:771), [scripts/install.sh:1994](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.nb1a8y/wt/scripts/install.sh:1994), [scripts/install.sh:3630](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-ga.nb1a8y/wt/scripts/install.sh:3630).** Reproduced on a fresh target with an unwritable `.github/`: `.claude/` and `docs/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md` were installed before CODEOWNERS staging failed. The run exited 1, but left the partial tree with neither manifest nor install-state because rollback covers only a previously backed-up `.claude/`. Minimal fix for 1.4.1: reserve all staging destinations before mutation or maintain a rollback ledger covering every written surface. Operationally, any nonzero install must cause the whole target to be restored or discarded.
