   109	# _framework_target_entries — the top-level target relpaths (files + dirs),
   110	# profile-aware, sorted + deduped. This is the STATIC intended set; it does not
   111	# touch disk (so install and upgrade derive an identical list regardless of
   112	# what is currently present).
   113	_framework_target_entries() {
   114	  {
   115	    # rail round-3 F1 — PATHNAME EXPANSION IS OFF for this whole enumeration.
   116	    # Every unquoted expansion below (FMS_PROFILE_PARTS, the delivered-template
   117	    # list before the cure) is fed from the environment, and word splitting is
   118	    # WANTED there while globbing never is. `set -f` separates the two: it
   119	    # disables pathname expansion and leaves splitting intact. MEASURED
   120	    # pre-cure: `FMS_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES='docs/*'` with the repo root as cwd
   121	    # recorded 125 unrelated files as framework-owned. Restored below so the
   122	    # option never leaks to a caller that reaches this function directly (the
   123	    # brace group is the left side of a pipeline, hence a subshell today — the
   124	    # save/restore is what keeps that true after a refactor).
