     1	# PLAN-183 W5 — delivery route table. THIS FILE IS THE TRUTH for its three
     2	# readers (the manifest generator, the upgrader and doctor); scripts/install.sh's
     3	# writers still carry their destinations in code, and CI checks that PARITY
     4	# (D3) instead of deriving it (v1.4.0-rc.1 conditions 8 and 62).
     5	# Destination relpath -> (source relpath, transformation). Reasoning lives
     6	# in PLAN-183 §8.5.1/§8.5.2; for the readers above the values live ONLY here.
     7	# A second copy in bash or Python that DECIDES ownership would be the "local
     8	# branch" CLAUDE.md §4 forbids; the installer's copies deliver, they do not decide.
     9	# Writers in scripts/install.sh (re-measured for v1.4.0-rc.1, round 11): the
    10	# functions install_docs_template, install_docs_templates and
    11	# install_github_templates; CODEOWNERS is rendered by _render_owner_handle
    12	# (no sed). Line numbers move — locate the SYMBOLS, not a line. Both
    13	# delivery functions are gated on CEREMONY != user.
    14	# Conventions: transform = "identity" (verbatim cp) or "substitute:<token>".
    15	#   flag_dep = the install.sh flag the route depends on; "-" = unconditional,
    16	#   "!github-owner" = the else-branch taken when the flag is ABSENT.
    17	# WARNING: .github/CODEOWNERS and .github/CODEOWNERS.template are MUTUALLY
    18	#   EXCLUSIVE (install.sh --github-owner takes the CODEOWNERS branch, its absence
    19	#   the .template branch): one run delivers one of the two, never both — and a
    20	#   `user` ceremony, a missing source or a preserved destination deliver fewer
    21	#   than the remaining routes. A table keyed by DESTINATION needs both rows anyway.
    22	# note carries PROSE ONLY. Structured values live in columns.
    23	dest	src	transform	flag_dep	origin	note
