   593	# --- rail round-7 F2: PHYSICAL confinement of the SOURCE --------------------
   594	# The destination side has had physical confinement since round 1 F2; the
   595	# SOURCE side had only the lexical predicate, and `[ -f ]`, `cp`, `cat` and
   596	# `sha256` all FOLLOW symlinks. MEASURED pre-cure (S327): with
   597	# `templates/docs/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md` a symlink to a regular file outside the
   598	# checkout, `[ -f ]` answered true and the delivered bytes hashed IDENTICAL to
   599	# the foreign file — foreign content installed into an adopter tree as
   600	# framework content, with the manifest then recording it as framework-owned.
   601	# A symlinked ANCESTOR (`templates/docs -> /elsewhere`) does the same thing and
   602	# passes every per-path lexical check.
   603	#
   604	# Two independent walls, both required:
   605	#   1. NO SYMLINK COMPONENT — every component of $2 under the physical root is
   606	#      tested with `-L`, leaf included. A real checkout of this framework has
   607	#      ZERO symlinks (measured: 0 under templates/, .claude/, docs/, and 0 in
   608	#      the whole tree excluding .git), so this costs production nothing.
   609	#   2. PHYSICAL CONTAINMENT — the deepest EXISTING ancestor of the source must
   610	#      resolve (cd -P/pwd -P; the bash 3.2 floor has no realpath) under the
   611	#      PHYSICALLY resolved root. "Deepest existing", not "the parent", so a
   612	#      source that is simply ABSENT — the `--pin` lane, where the destination
   613	#      list is this upgrader's and the sources are the pin's — still reaches
   614	#      its caller's `-f` test and keeps its "SKIPPED (source missing)" verdict
   615	#      instead of being renamed into a confinement refusal.
   616	#
   617	# $1 = source root (absolute). $2 = source relpath.
   618	# rc 0 = usable. rc 1 = refuse, with the reason in _WBM_SRC_CONFINE_WHY (a
   619	# refusal nobody can NAME is the silence D3 was made of).
   620	_WBM_SRC_CONFINE_WHY=""
